// Cognito sign-up abuse and the discovery sweep after it
// ARTEX detections by ThreatDefence. Source: https://threatdefence.com/article/artex-agentic-attack-framework-detection-hunting
// Example hunt for Microsoft Sentinel and Defender XDR advanced hunting. Test and baseline before alerting.
// Every ARTEX session Datadog reviewed opened with unauthenticated S3 reads. In CloudTrail data events these have a `userIdentity.type` of `AWSAccount` and an `accountId` of `anonymous`. Check S3 data events or server access logs for anonymous `GetObject` and `ListObjects` calls, and for the placeholder object names listed above.
// Hunts 10 to 13 are **example** KQL for Microsoft Defender for Endpoint advanced hunting. Hunts 14 to 16 are example KQL for Microsoft Sentinel. Adapt and test them the same way.

// Example: bursts of Cognito sign-up and recovery calls from one source
AWSCloudTrail
| where TimeGenerated >= datetime(2026-08-01)
| where EventSource == "cognito-idp.amazonaws.com"
| where EventName in ("SignUp", "InitiateAuth", "ForgotPassword", "ResendConfirmationCode", "RespondToAuthChallenge")
| summarize Calls=count(), Errors=countif(isnotempty(ErrorCode)), Events=make_set(EventName),
    Agents=make_set(UserAgent, 10)
    by SourceIpAddress, bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)
| where Calls >= 30
| order by Calls desc

// Example: a Cognito-issued identity trying many discovery calls that are denied
AWSCloudTrail
| where TimeGenerated >= datetime(2026-08-01)
| where UserIdentityArn has "CognitoIdentityCredentials"
| where ErrorCode has "AccessDenied" or ErrorCode has "Unauthorized"
| summarize Denied=count(), Actions=dcount(EventName), Sample=make_set(EventName, 25)
    by UserIdentityArn, SourceIpAddress, bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)
| where Actions >= 8
| order by Denied desc
